        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the point $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\cos\\theta+h,\\,y=b\\sin\\theta+k,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the ellipse is centered at the point $(4,0),$ $a=3$ and $b=7.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=3\\cos\\theta+4,\\,y=7\\sin\\theta,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"
